<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield falls to 23.19 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield falls to 23.19 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of three-month GKO discount Treasury bills fell to 23.19 percent at an auction on April 8 from 24.40 percent at the last auction on April 1, the National Bank said.</p>
<p>Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   April 8	    April 1</p>
<p> Series number		 KZ43K1007972    KZ43K0307977</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)		500		  500</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, bln tenge)	    1,68		 0,83</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million tenge)	     500		  471</p>
<p> Average price (pct)		   94.52		94.25</p>
<p> Average yield (pct)		   23.19		24.40</p>
<p> Tenor				   91 days	    91 days</p>
<p> Maturity			     July 10, 1997    July 3, 1997</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
